.TH "netom\-bmpdump" "1" "FastNetMon Inc"
.SH NAME
netom\-bmpdump \- offline BMP, BGP and EVPN capture decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netom\-bmpdump
.BI \-r " FILE"
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads PCAP or PCAPNG captures, reassembles TCP streams, and displays BMP
messages and their BGP/EVPN contents. It runs without a Netom daemon,
TShark, Python, or root privileges.
.PP
Each output record represents one BMP message. Multiple messages in one
packet are separated and split messages are reassembled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-r " FILE" "\fR, \fB\-\-read " FILE
Read a capture. Use a dash for standard input.
.TP
.BI \-p " PORT" "\fR, \fB\-\-port " PORT
Select a BMP TCP port. Repeat to select multiple ports.
Replaces the default ports 11019 and 1790.
.TP
.BI \-c " COUNT" "\fR, \fB\-\-count " COUNT
Stop after this many matching BMP messages.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Print readable message blocks with every route.
Use \fB\-vv\fR to also print the complete decoded JSON.
.TP
.B \-n
Numeric addresses, which are always enabled.
.TP
.B \-j\fR, \fB\-\-json
Print newline-delimited JSON. JSON output never contains ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Only print aggregate counts. Combine with \fB\-\-json\fR for a JSON summary.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Control ANSI colors. The default, auto, requires a recognized color terminal
and honors NO_COLOR. Always explicitly overrides automatic detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-router " ADDRESS"
Filter by the BMP exporter's source IP address.
.TP
.BI \-\-peer " ADDRESS"
Filter by the monitored BGP peer's IP address.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " TYPE"
Filter by route-monitoring, statistics, peer-down, peer-up, initiation,
termination, or route-mirroring.
.TP
.B \-\-evpn
Only messages containing EVPN NLRI.
.TP
.BI \-\-route-type " 1|2|3|4|5"
Only messages containing this EVPN route type.
.TP
.B \-\-add-path
Force ADD-PATH for supported families when Peer Up negotiation is missing.
Use only when those families are known to use ADD-PATH.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Show the Netom release version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
netom-bmpdump -r capture.pcapng --evpn -v
netom-bmpdump -r capture.pcapng --route-type 5 -j
netom-bmpdump -r capture.pcapng --summary
netom-bmpdump -r capture.pcapng -v --color always | less -R
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: clean completion.
.br
2: read/decode errors or diagnostics; partial output may still be useful.
.br
130: interrupted.
.SH LIMITATIONS
IP fragment reassembly, encrypted transport, IPv6 jumbograms, and extended
BGP OPEN optional-parameter encoding are not implemented. Checksums are not
validated. Missing TCP data is reported. Unknown protocol fields are
retained as raw hexadecimal data in JSON.
.PP
Capture timestamps use UTC and identify the packet completing reassembly.
Filters select whole messages, including other routes in a matching message.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable automatic coloring.
.TP
.B TERM
Used for terminal color detection.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Override the output width, bounded to 60 through 120 columns.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netom (1),
.BR netom-cli (1),
.BR tcpdump (8)
